    <DataNode elementId="N-Acylsphingosine" textLabel="an N-acylsphingosine" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="52639" dataSource="ChEBI" />
      <Graphics centerX="500" centerY="400" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="AU4FS-1, PMN, zhang, SRI, caspi">A |FRAME: N-Acylsphingosine &quot;sphingosine ceramide&quot;| is |FRAME: Ceramides| molecule that is composed of |FRAME: SPHINGOSINE| and |FRAME: Fatty-Acids|. This type of ceramide is common in animals, and is produced by desaturation of a sphinganine base within a ceramide (known as |FRAME: CPD3DJ-82|) by |FRAME: EC-1.14.19.17|. Ceramides are found in high concentrations within the cell membrane and are one of the component lipids that make up |FRAME: Sphingomyelins sphingomyelin|, one of the major lipids in the lipid bilayer.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="N-Acylsphingosine" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Metanetx" value="MNXM104" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_LigandCpd" value="C00195" />
